---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { YOUTUBE_TERMS_URL } from '../lib/watch/contract';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What Dangerous Robot keeps about you, who can read it, and how to remove it." layout="reading">
  <article class="reading">
    <Breadcrumb crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Privacy' },
    ]} />
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      What we keep about you, who can read it, and how to remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>Reading the site</h2>
    <p>
      The site runs no analytics or tracking scripts. The one exception is the <a href="#watch">Watch page</a>, which loads images and video from YouTube. Display settings, such as theme and text size, are saved only in your browser.
    </p>

    {/* Draft wording: Brandon to review the "Reading the site" exception sentence and this section. */}
    <h2 id="watch">Watching videos</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/watch">Watch page</a> lists videos from YouTube. Its thumbnails and hover previews load from YouTube's image servers (i.ytimg.com), so YouTube (Google) receives your IP address when you open the page or hover over a video.
    </p>
    <p>
      The video player loads only when you press Play or pick a video. It comes from youtube-nocookie.com, and once it loads, YouTube's own policies apply, including anything it stores in your browser. Your hover previews setting is saved only in your browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      The video list comes from YouTube API Services. See the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href={YOUTUBE_TERMS_URL}>YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="petitions">Petitions</h2>
    <p>
      We use your email only to confirm your signature. We never show it, share it, or send you anything else.
    </p>

    <h3>What we keep when you sign</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name.</li>
      <li>Your email address.</li>
      <li>Whether you want your name shown on the public list of signers.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your IP address is used for a moment to slow down repeat attempts. It is not saved with your signature.
    </p>

    <h3>Who can read it</h3>
    <p>
      Only Dangerous Robot. Cloudflare stores the list, and Resend delivers the confirmation email. The public list shows only the names of signers who chose to be listed.
    </p>

    <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A signature that is never confirmed is deleted after 7 days.</li>
      <li>When a petition closes, we delete its signers' email addresses. Names and the count stay.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Removing your signature</h3>
    <p>
      Use the removal link in your confirmation email, or write to <a href="mailto:contact@dangerousrobot.org">contact@dangerousrobot.org</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  article h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  article h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
